--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -33,6 +33,21 @@ applyPatch({ foo: ['bar', 'baz'] }, [{ op: 'add', path: '/foo/1', value: 'qux' }
 // => { foo: ['bar', 'qux', 'baz'] }
 ```
 
+### JSON Patch diffing
+
+`createPatch(from, to)` compares two JSON documents and returns a [JSON
+Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902) that turns `from` into `to` when applied with
+`applyPatch`. It describes only what changed — object members that were added, removed or changed,
+and the differing span of an array — instead of replacing the whole document. `from` and `to` are
+left untouched.
+
+```ts
+import { createPatch } from 'json-toolkit';
+
+createPatch({ foo: 'bar', baz: 1 }, { foo: 'bar', baz: 2 });
+// => [{ op: 'replace', path: '/baz', value: 2 }]
+```
+
 ### JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
 
 `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies a [JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386)
